WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:03.300
We see the struggles of others unfold around us,

00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:05.600
as they fight for the things important to them.

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:10.100
There's a man who fights on behalf of his broken homeland,

00:00:10.829 --> 00:00:13.700
Another who fights to prevent his kingdom being broken.

00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:17.100
One man believes in research for the sake of knowledge,

00:00:17.800 --> 00:00:20.900
and maybe this knowledge will give you the power to fix your mistake.

00:00:21.670 --> 00:00:24.600
With this power you may have to do terrible things to many,

00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:26.800
to save the lives of many more.

00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:29.700
How can the gods be so cruel?

00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:33.200
To stand idly by, while the powerless have everything taken from them.

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:35.700
Perhaps if you give them something,

00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:37.600
then they'll give you something in return?

00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:41.500
Surely there's a reward for faithfully serving the gods of this land.

00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:45.100
Or perhaps you'll be cast aside to fade from memory.

00:00:45.220 --> 00:00:48.020
A fool, who dared to believe in something greater,

00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:52.410
without ever knowing that your final acts, could've changed fate.

00:00:56.840 --> 00:00:58.610
Man is born from the dark,

00:00:58.610 --> 00:01:02.729
A soul that is kindled, flickers, dwindles and dies in the shadow of his Gods.

00:01:03.400 --> 00:01:06.549
The human form is fragile and death
comes quickly,

00:01:06.549 --> 00:01:10.600
but the Spirit is strong and it clings to
life like only a mortal can.

00:01:11.509 --> 00:01:14.300
So in a way man was not designed to
become undead.

00:01:14.500 --> 00:01:16.800
Fear of death Is what lets us live.

00:01:17.300 --> 00:01:20.100
Take that away, and humanity becomes harder to hold on to.

00:01:20.490 --> 00:01:23.100
Without humanity, you could become more hollow than man.

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:26.899
Yet an undead who would die for something has nothing to fear,

00:01:26.899 --> 00:01:30.400
for death simply becomes a stepping
stone to his goal.

00:01:33.909 --> 00:01:38.060
If you fall down seven times, stand up
eight. That's the cry of the undead.

00:01:38.060 --> 00:01:41.670
It's not a matter of life or death
that's about what breaks first - your will,

00:01:41.670 --> 00:01:43.780
or the barriers in your way.

00:01:43.780 --> 00:01:48.300
Everyone has their own paths to face.
"H-have you seen my father?

00:01:48.300 --> 00:01:51.510
You wouldn't miss him. A suit of armor, just like mine?"

00:01:51.510 --> 00:01:54.930
"Friend, I have an idea - a good one, really.

00:01:54.930 --> 00:01:59.300
I will rush those dire fiends and you can slip away in the confusion!.."

00:02:00.100 --> 00:02:02.700
"Why..? Why..?

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:06.900
After all this searching, I still cannot find it.

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:10.920
Was it all a lie? Have I done this all for nothing?"

00:02:11.800 --> 00:02:14.100
[coughs] "All of you..

00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:18.020
forgive me. For I have availed you nothing."

00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:20.000
"I'm finished..

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:21.370
We're both on the brink you see?

00:02:21.370 --> 00:02:24.090
End of story. You bloody fool."

00:02:24.600 --> 00:02:30.000
"Regrettably, I have failed in my mission. But perhaps you can keep the torch lit..."

00:02:30.210 --> 00:02:32.200
"There is an old saying in my family:

00:02:32.800 --> 00:02:34.800
Thou who art undead art Chosen.

00:02:35.200 --> 00:02:37.600
In thine exodus from the Undead Asylum,

00:02:37.700 --> 00:02:40.600
maketh pilgrimage to the land of Ancient Lords.

00:02:40.820 --> 00:02:42.600
When thou ringeth the bell of awakening,

00:02:43.300 --> 00:02:46.000
the fate of the undead, thou shalt know."

00:02:46.300 --> 00:02:47.400
"Well now you know.

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:50.100
And I can die with hope in my heart."

00:02:51.200 --> 00:02:53.100
So do we fight for one man who fell?

00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:56.100
No. We fight for the many who fell before us,

00:02:56.300 --> 00:02:59.550
for the souls of nameless soldiers, warriors and heroes.

00:02:59.900 --> 00:03:03.980
Did you ring the second bell? That is incredible, I must say..

00:03:03.980 --> 00:03:08.900
I cannot do it myself. I lack the strength, and the bravery..

00:03:09.340 --> 00:03:10.380
But you...

00:03:11.020 --> 00:03:14.100
Finally the curse of the undead will be lifted..

00:03:14.900 --> 00:03:17.500
and I can die human...

00:03:17.600 --> 00:03:18.500
Please,

00:03:18.700 --> 00:03:20.400
save us all.

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:24.660
Please.

